# The proxy PC's Caddy for the internet server (design.md 6.17): TLS for the owner's domain, and every request over
# the LAN to the GPU PC's server (serve.public.example.toml: port 8001; its trusted-proxies is THIS PC's LAN address).
# Caddy 2.7 or later. Edit the lines marked EDIT, then: caddy run --config Caddyfile (or caddy reload --config Caddyfile).
#
# - TLS: Caddy gets and renews the certificate for the domain by itself (ports 80 and 443 must reach this PC, and the
#   domain's DNS A/AAAA record must point to it).
# - X-Forwarded-For: reverse_proxy sets it to the address the request came from. An internet client is not one of
#   Caddy's own trusted_proxies (none are set here), so a header the client sent is dropped, not passed on. The GPU
#   PC's server reads the header only from this PC, from the right.
# - Streams: a response of Content-Type text/event-stream is flushed at once, by Caddy's own rule; flush_interval is
#   left alone (a negative one would also keep the GPU writing for a client that has left).
# - Timeouts: none on the server's answer. A 32,768-token prompt takes 22.5 s to its first token and an 8,192-token
#   reply minutes more; a stream gets ": ping" every 15 s until its first token, and a request that is not streamed
#   gets nothing until its reply is whole. An idle connection to the server is closed after 60 s (keepalive), before
#   the server's own 120 s (idle-timeout), so that Caddy never sends a request on a connection the server is closing.
# - While the GPU PC's supervisor restarts the server, a refused connection is tried again for up to 15 s
#   (lb_try_duration: only a connection that failed, so no request reaches the server twice).
# - Bodies: 32 MiB at most (413), as the server's max-body-mb.
# - /metrics and /debug are not served from the internet (the server answers /metrics to the GPU PC itself only).
# - No access log (Caddy writes none unless a `log` directive asks): the GPU PC keeps the metadata (ZDR).

{
	# EDIT (optional): an address for the certificate authority's notices
	email you@example.com
	servers {
		timeouts {
			read_header 30s
			read_body 10m
			idle 5m
		}
	}
}

# EDIT: the owner's domain
llm.example.com {
	request_body {
		max_size 32MiB
	}

	@inside path /metrics /metrics/* /debug /debug/*
	respond @inside 404

	# EDIT: the GPU PC's LAN address
	reverse_proxy 192.168.0.20:8001 {
		lb_try_duration 15s
		lb_try_interval 500ms
		transport http {
			dial_timeout 5s
			keepalive 60s
		}
	}
}
